diff -ruN '--exclude=.git' a/research/p01-p03-foundations/report.md b/research/p01-p03-foundations/report.md
--- a/research/p01-p03-foundations/report.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/research/p01-p03-foundations/report.md	2026-08-05 19:27:55.205975761 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# P01-P03 implementation report
+
+The reference implementation passed its complete standard-library core test suite under the race detector. The primary conformance run examined 720 merge schedules and produced one canonical state, examined six candidate completion orders and produced one selected view, while a first-two-arrivals policy produced six distinct views. One hundred concurrent retry runs produced zero divergences. A deliberately conflicting fact ID retained both variants and failed verification rather than selecting one by timing.
+
+The provenance fixture contains three facts, four derivations, and two observations. The selected claim has two independent derivations and least proof rank one. The proof bundle verifies independently, while an altered payload retaining the original ID is detected as tampering.
+
+The implementation comparison is not a general benchmark. It isolates a known cost of the immutable reference API: repeated one-record `Join` clones the accumulated state. At 2,000 facts the primary run measured 1,089.8 ms for repeated persistent join and 3.3 ms for the mutable ledger, with equal output. Median scaling results are in `results/scaling.json`. The result justifies keeping the pure operation as a specification and using a mutable builder at ingestion boundaries.
+
+The complete repository test suite was not run because the supplied `go.mod` requires Go 1.26.5 and uses syntax unsupported by the available Go 1.23.2 toolchain. Production adapters and cache migrations therefore have static parse and call-arity evidence but still require execution in the repository's declared toolchain before merge.
